        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: update dependencies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's workspace dependency set had accumulated routine version drift, while several newest releases changed APIs, peers, platform support, or Node engine ranges. Updating only the lockfile would leave publishable shrinkwraps and integration contracts stale.\n\nCloses #99952.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Refresh direct dependencies across the root package, packages, UI, and plugins.\n- Regenerate the pnpm lockfile and publishable npm shrinkwraps.\n- Adapt the affected ACP, grammY, Pierre diffs, Codex, and Copilot integration contracts.\n- Remove the obsolete Claude ACP patch and the no-longer-direct Pierre theme dependency.\n- Keep explicit holds where the newest release conflicts with OpenClaw's supported Node, peer, or platform matrix.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers receive current compatible dependency releases without changing OpenClaw configuration or public APIs. Codex model metadata, Telegram bot metadata, ACP completion handling, and the diffs renderer remain aligned with their updated upstream contracts.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused ACPX, Codex, Copilot, diffs, Docker, Telegram, and plugin dependency-contract shards pass.\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx`, peer checks, dependency pin/patch/shrinkwrap guards, and the vulnerability gate pass.\n- Direct Codex source inspection plus a live harness `model/list` probe confirmed the managed version and public model snapshot.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview completed with no accepted/actionable findings after the final cleanup.\n- Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox proof is running as `tbx_01kwpj2dzvn8xq0k7hwdxhky8y`; completion is required before merge.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
